## Description

Reading an unfinished, index-less `.mcap` file directly through `rosbag2_py.SequentialReader` corrupts the second message's payload without reporting a read error.

The root cause is a shared-buffer overwrite: `MCAPStorage` holds a pointer to the pending message's payload, then `read_metadata()` reuses the same buffer before the payload is copied.

Conditions observed:
- **No message index:** Reading falls back to file order.
- **Standalone file:** The same file reads correctly inside a directory with `metadata.yaml`, and after `ros2 bag reindex`.
- **Uncompressed chunk:** The chunk's `compression` is `""`. This includes chunks left uncompressed when compression saves less than 2%. Actually zstd-compressed chunks read correctly.
- **Message 2 only:** Corruption occurs when message 2 begins a chunk. This happens when message 1 fills the first chunk (at least 768 KiB, `mcap::DefaultChunkSize`). Small-message tests did not reproduce it because message 2 fell outside the overwritten region.

## Expected Behavior

`read_next()` returns every message's payload exactly as stored.

## Actual Behavior

Message 2's first 423 bytes are replaced with bytes from the file's `rosbag2` Metadata record. Deserializing the affected `sensor_msgs/PointCloud2` message fails.

Byte-level evidence:
- The test file contained 100,000-point `PointCloud2` messages (1,600,141 bytes serialized), recorded at 10 Hz and terminated with `SIGKILL`.
- Of 26 complete messages, all matched the Python MCAP reader except message 2.
- Message 2's bytes `[0, 422]` differ and match `file[122:545]`, which contains the Metadata record body.
- In the minimal C++ reproduction, `message.data` is at `0x…6057`, while `ReadRecord` returns `record.data` at `0x…6010`: the same buffer, offset by 71 bytes. The 494-byte record overwrites 423 bytes of the pending payload.

## To Reproduce

1. Publish `sensor_msgs/PointCloud2` messages containing 100,000 points at 10 Hz.
2. Run `ros2 bag record -s mcap -o bag /lidar/points`.
3. Kill the recorder with `SIGKILL` after a few seconds, leaving `bag/bag_0.mcap` without a summary, index, or `metadata.yaml`.
4. Open the file directly using `rosbag2_py.SequentialReader` and deserialize each message as `PointCloud2`. Deserialization fails on message 2.

A Python reproduction of the read failure:

```python
import rosbag2_py
from rclpy.serialization import deserialize_message
from sensor_msgs.msg import PointCloud2

r = rosbag2_py.SequentialReader()
r.open(
    rosbag2_py.StorageOptions(
        uri="bag/bag_0.mcap",
        storage_id="mcap",
    ),
    rosbag2_py.ConverterOptions("cdr", "cdr"),
)

while r.has_next():
    deserialize_message(r.read_next()[1], PointCloud2)
```

### Minimal libmcap Reproducer

This reproduces the buffer overwrite using the vendored libmcap library alone, without rosbag2.

<details>
<summary>alias.cpp</summary>

```cpp
// g++ -std=c++17 -I/opt/ros/jazzy/include/mcap_vendor alias.cpp -L/opt/ros/jazzy/lib -Wl,-rpath,/opt/ros/jazzy/lib -lmcap -o alias
// Usage: ./alias <file.mcap> [interleave]

#include <mcap/reader.hpp>

#include <cstdio>
#include <cstring>
#include <fstream>
#include <vector>

int main(int argc, char ** argv)
{
  const bool interleave = argc > 2 && std::strcmp(argv[2], "interleave") == 0;
  std::ifstream input(argv[1], std::ios::binary);
  mcap::FileStreamReader source(input);
  mcap::McapReader reader;

  if (auto s = reader.open(source); !s.ok()) {
    std::printf("open: %s\n", s.message.c_str());
    return 1;
  }
  if (auto s = reader.readSummary(mcap::ReadSummaryMethod::AllowFallbackScan); !s.ok()) {
    std::printf("readSummary: %s\n", s.message.c_str());
    return 1;
  }

  mcap::ReadMessageOptions options;
  options.readOrder = mcap::ReadMessageOptions::ReadOrder::FileOrder;
  auto onProblem = [](const mcap::Status & s) {
    std::printf("problem: %s\n", s.message.c_str());
  };
  auto view = reader.readMessages(onProblem, options);
  auto it = view.begin();
  ++it;  // now on message 2, like rosbag2 after enqueueing message 1

  const auto & msg = it->message;
  std::vector<std::byte> before(msg.data, msg.data + msg.dataSize);
  std::printf("message 2: dataSize=%lu data=%p\n",
              (unsigned long)msg.dataSize,
              static_cast<const void *>(msg.data));

  if (interleave) {
    // What MCAPStorage::read_metadata() does for each "rosbag2" metadata index.
    for (const auto & [name, index] : reader.metadataIndexes()) {
      mcap::Record record;
      auto s = mcap::McapReader::ReadRecord(source, index.offset, &record);
      std::printf("ReadRecord(%s @ %lu): %s, record.data=%p size=%lu\n",
                  name.c_str(), (unsigned long)index.offset,
                  s.ok() ? "ok" : s.message.c_str(),
                  static_cast<const void *>(record.data),
                  (unsigned long)record.dataSize);
    }
  }

  std::vector<std::byte> after(msg.data, msg.data + msg.dataSize);
  size_t first = 0, count = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < before.size(); ++i) {
    if (before[i] != after[i] && count++ == 0) {
      first = i;
    }
  }
  if (count == 0) {
    std::printf("message 2 payload unchanged\n");
  } else {
    std::printf("message 2 payload CHANGED: %zu bytes differ from offset %zu\n",
                count, first);
  }
  return count == 0 ? 0 : 2;
}
```

</details>

Compile and run:

```bash
g++ -std=c++17 \
  -I/opt/ros/jazzy/include/mcap_vendor \
  alias.cpp \
  -L/opt/ros/jazzy/lib \
  -Wl,-rpath,/opt/ros/jazzy/lib \
  -lmcap -o alias

./alias bag_0.mcap interleave
```

The program exits with code `2` and prints `message 2 payload CHANGED`. Without `interleave`, or against a file whose chunks are actually zstd-compressed, the payload remains unchanged.

## System

- OS: Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble), `ros:jazzy-ros-base` container
- ROS 2 Distro: Jazzy
- Install Method: APT
- `ros-jazzy-rosbag2-storage-mcap`: `0.26.11-1noble.20260911.143733`
- MCAP vendor: 0.26.11, C++ v1.3.1

## Additional Context

Traced at [[rosbag2 commit cb8fa198](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/tree/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/tree/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b) and [[MCAP commit 1a64fd40](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/tree/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e)](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/tree/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e).

1. In the [[standalone-file path](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_cpp/src/rosbag2_cpp/readers/sequential_reader.cpp#L118-L123)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_cpp/src/rosbag2_cpp/readers/sequential_reader.cpp#L118-L123), read-order selection fails without an index and falls back to file order. `reset_iterator()` reads and enqueues message 1, then advances the iterator to message 2 ([[copy](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L559)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L559), [[advance](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L565)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L565)).
2. In file-order reading, MCAP's [`[ReadRecord](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L1238)`](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L1238) reuses `FileStreamReader::buffer_` ([[buffer read](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L116)](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L116)). For uncompressed chunks, `BufferReader::reset` retains a pointer to the chunk records ([[lines 20–25](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L20-L25)](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L20-L25)). The indexed path instead copies uncompressed chunks into their own storage ([[lines 1871–1873](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L1871-L1873)](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L1871-L1873)).
3. `SequentialReader::open()` then calls `get_metadata()` ([[line 125](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_cpp/src/rosbag2_cpp/readers/sequential_reader.cpp#L125)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_cpp/src/rosbag2_cpp/readers/sequential_reader.cpp#L125)). `MCAPStorage::read_metadata()` calls `ReadRecord` on the same data source ([[rosbag2 line 423](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L423)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L423)), overwriting the buffer ([[MCAP record-body read](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L680)](https://github.com/foxglove/mcap/blob/1a64fd40358998775b27fee516a28e07a97db27e/cpp/mcap/include/mcap/reader.inl#L680)).
4. The next `has_next()` copies message 2 from the overwritten buffer ([`[mcap_storage.cpp](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L559)`](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/cb8fa198b93bfed90e2417b52b8645fb9ef89c2b/rosbag2_storage_mcap/src/mcap_storage.cpp#L559)).

In directory mode, `load_current_file()` resets the iterator after metadata loading and does not read the file afterward, which explains why the same file reads correctly.

The same relevant code exists in [[Rolling](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/tree/b9e134ba548921e5fcf23b2861f31295d3800496)](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/tree/b9e134ba548921e5fcf23b2861f31295d3800496), verified by source inspection but not runtime-tested.

## Possible Fixes

- Give `read_metadata()` its own data source.
- Read metadata before creating the message iterator in the standalone-file path.
- Reset the iterator after `get_metadata()`.
- Copy the payload before advancing the iterator, avoiding a pending `MessageView` that references mutable shared storage.
